Considering the count=24 sequence of values which are equiv 18
modulo 19, things start to explode.  The count=24 values in the
"times 2 modulo 7436429" sequences become 2 sequences of
count=264 and one of count=24.  One of the count=264 sequences
consists of (30*k-1) values which are not divisible by 23
The count=24 sequence of (30*k-1) values is equivalent to 22
modulo 23
 
Things start to explode, but also this means that there are many
sequences that are valid to explore up where there could exist
sequences of length up to 29 (next prime above 23..).

