I can see that for chains where the values are equivalent
to 89,149,179 (mod 210), but not equivalent to 989,1649,1979
(mod 2310), then the maximum chain length is 9 since the cycle
of values mod 11 has size 10,
I can also see that for chains where the values are equiv 209
(mod 210) but not equivalent to 2309 (mod 2310), then the
maximum chain length is 11 since the cycles of values mod 13
has size 12.
There is further working to be done in this context to consider
further chain length maximums as we move further into the sieve
options but also further thinking.  The "search" for chains of
longer lengths by searching through (30.k-1) values which are
equivalent to various values module p# could be considered in
a more systematic fashion.

Could add to cunningham-chain-type1.py script to include checking
of values modulo p# and information about identified maximum
cycle lengths

