22 Feb 26
Primes which are = 1 (mod 6) are not Sophie Germain primes, form
type 1 Cunningham chains of length 1
For primes which are = 11, 17 or 23 (mod 30) these can only ever
form type 1 Cunningham  chains of length at most 3, except for
11, 23, 47 which form a chain of length 5, namely 2, 5, 11, 23,
47.  Starting at 30.k+11, the sequence continues 30.2.k+23,
30.(4.k+1)+17 and the next item in the sequence is composite,
30(8.k+3)+5
For primes = 29 (mod 30), if the primes are also = 1 or 3 (mod
7)
then these can only form type 1 Cunningham chains of length at
most 2, for example the chain 29 = 1 (mod 7), 59 = 3 (mod 7),
119=7.17, since for a prime p_i = 3 (mod 7), then p-{i+1} =
2.p_i+1 = 0 (mod 7).
For primes =2,4,5,6 (mod 7) then these can form longer chains..

