18 Mar 26
sqrt(10000*30*2^4) = 2190.89
So scripting the above method will require some improvements
The method has found the chains of length 6 that were originally
reported by Cunningham.  But the first chain of length 7 is 1122659

sqrt(1122659*2^6) = 8476.45

If we are searching for chains of a specific length, then as 30k
increases, then so should the values with which to sieve, ie. for chains
of length 6 then we need to consider the primes less than sqrt(30k.2^5)
to ensure that we sieve values fully.  As the desired chain length and
the size of 30k values increase, then it won't be possible to sieve
completely.
