I have thoughts about how to improve the processing of sieve set
members.
sieve_vals is a set
sieve_to is a collection
All the values of sieve_to.values() are compared to the current k
value and if any of the values are less than k, then values are
added to the sieve_vals set.
The logic and flow of the script needs checking and improvement.
I think the sieve_to data structure, might be better off
being set up as an ordered list and so the lowest sieve_to value
is immediately known and values can be added to the sieve_vals
until the sieve_to values are all greater than k.

