Describe the algorithm for determining primes with 2 as a
primitive root and the order of 2 mod p from determining the
factors of Mersenne numbers
2 3 3
3 7 7
4 15=3.5 5
5 31 31
6 63=3^2.7 -
7 127 127
8 255=3.5.17 17
9 511=7.73 73
10 1023=3.11.31 11

Start with M_2=3 implies that the order of 2 mod 3 is 2 and so 2
is a primitive root for 3
M_3=7 implies that the order of 2 mod 7 is 3
M_4=15.  4 is divisible by 2, so M_4 is divisible by M_2.  15/3=5
so the order of 2 mod 5 is 4. 2 is a primitive root of 5
M_5=31, and 31 is prime. The order of 2 mod 31 is 5
M_6=63. Consider factors of 6. M_2|M_6 and M_3|M_6. Also 6=2.M_2

